\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1  \cf0  Be removed, ye hills and mountains,
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   God's great kindness shall not cease,
\par   All who drink at God's blest fountain
\par   share His covenant of peace,
\par   This I know: I shall not fear;
\par   my redeemer draweth near!
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He has promised all who fear Him
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   shall their comfort find in God.
\par   Terror shall not dare come near him
\par   who the righteous way has trod.
\par   This my song shall ever be:
\par   My Redeemer loveth me.
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.   This word gives strength to the weary
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   and to comfort those in grief;
\par   they shall have all peace they require
\par     that is over what man thinks,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0   if you have this as your weapon
\par   there is nothing to be feared.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  God will free from dark oppression
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0   those bowed down in pain and grief
\par   lift the soul from deep depression;
\par  those who ask shall find relief.
\par  My Redeemer will not fail
\par  and His promise shall prevail
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  Give me, Lord, all that is needed
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Thy word to accept in joy.
\par  Fear of death has not succeeded,
\par  faith and trust in thee destroy.
\par  I need never know distress
\par  if I do my Lord confess.\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

